diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..ee1456d 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,44 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Event delivery
+
+An event creates one delivery for each active webhook on its board that subscribes
+to the event's action. Deliveries are queued only after the event transaction
+commits. Generic endpoints receive a JSON POST containing `id`, `action`,
+`created_at`, `eventable` (the card or comment), `board`, and `creator`. Slack
+endpoints receive `text`; Campfire and Basecamp chat endpoints receive HTML
+`content`.
+
+Requests include:
+
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `X-Webhook-Id`: the stable delivery ID, suitable for receiver-side deduplication
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the request time in UTC
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body,
+  using the webhook's `signing_secret`
+
+Verify the signature against the raw body before processing an event. Use a
+constant-time comparison for signatures.
+
+Each delivery is attempted **once**, with no automatic retries. Duplicate jobs
+cannot send a second POST. HTTP 2xx responses count as success; other statuses
+(including redirects) count as failures. Timeouts and connection errors are logged
+as errors. Requests have a ten-second HTTP timeout, do not follow redirects, and
+cannot target private or reserved IP addresses.
+
+A single POST attempt is not an exactly-once processing guarantee: a timeout or
+worker crash may leave it unknown whether the receiver processed the request.
+An interrupted worker can leave a delivery `in_progress`; that delivery is not
+resent. Receivers needing exactly-once processing should durably deduplicate on
+`X-Webhook-Id` in the same transaction as their event processing.
+
+A webhook is automatically deactivated after at least ten consecutive failed
+deliveries when the failure streak has lasted at least one hour. Both conditions
+must be met. A successful delivery resets the streak. Reactivation also clears
+the streak, and queued deliveries are skipped if the webhook is inactive when
+they start.
+
+Delivery logs are retained for seven days. The scheduled cleanup removes older
+entries every fifteen minutes.
